  "conclusions": [
    "Own Triton grouped kernel vs torch.bmm: 2.8-6.5x faster at these shapes (bmm is a poor fit).",
    "FP8 vs our Triton bf16: 1.27-1.33x at the default 64x64x64 tile and 1.70x at the best dw13 tile 128x128x64 (358.1 TF fp8 vs 173.1 TF bf16); fp8 358.8 TF at 128x128x64.",
    "FP8 accuracy with per-expert scales is ~3.7e-2 max relative vs bf16 reference (e4m3 activation/gradient quantization) - too high for a naive swap; needs a per-token/block scale strategy or a training-tolerance test before integration.",
    "Production MoE dW segment is dw13 2.97 + dw 1.23 + dw_reduce 0.73 = 4.93 ms/step (~0.2475 ms/layer for dw13); this prototype's bf16 kernel is 0.104 ms/layer at the same shape, so even a bf16 grouped rewrite is worth trying before FP8.",
    "Next: integrate a bf16 grouped dW kernel with the production padded/NOPAD layout, A/B end-to-end; then add FP8 with a tolerance/training test."
  ]
